   "reply2": "Lie it on its side, so the 40 × 60 mm profile is flat on the bed and the 30 mm thickness points up. That needs no supports for the hook's curve and keeps the layer lines running along the profile, which makes it much stronger where the hook bends under load. I'm inferring the profile from the bounding box and haven't looked at the hole or fillet geometry, so check the overhangs in your slicer preview."
  },
