   },
   "reply2": "Print it lying on its side, flat on one of the 30 mm-wide faces. That puts the L-shaped profile in the print plane, so the layers run along the hook and plate and the load across the inside corner doesn't try to split them apart. It also needs no supports, because the profile is flat on the bed.\n\nStanding up would also print without supports, but the load would then pull the layers apart at that corner, which is the weakest direction for a print."
  }
